00:28:21.430 --> 00:28:26.755
So we want to basically make
everything sit in the center.

00:28:26.755 --> 00:28:29.950
On a phone, it'll
be like it is now.

00:28:29.950 --> 00:28:32.080
But on a big screen
like the viewer right

00:28:32.080 --> 00:28:34.120
here, that's not ideal.

00:28:34.120 --> 00:28:38.505
But to do that, we need
to go back into the HTML.

00:28:38.505 --> 00:28:44.060
And I want to see, how are we
going to target this whole app?

00:28:44.060 --> 00:28:47.230
So we have the
body of the thing.

00:28:47.230 --> 00:28:48.355
And then, we have this div.

00:28:48.355 --> 00:28:50.680
And that div contains
the whole app.

00:28:50.680 --> 00:28:53.720
And its class is
container-fluid.

00:28:53.720 --> 00:28:57.770
Which makes sense, because we're
using this fluid page here.

00:28:57.770 --> 00:29:01.810
And so what we can do is, target
this container-fluid class

00:29:01.810 --> 00:29:05.520
and just give it
a maximum width.

00:29:05.520 --> 00:29:09.570
And that should keep
things nice and centered.

00:29:09.570 --> 00:29:11.370
So I say, container-fluid.

00:29:15.190 --> 00:29:17.020
Fluid.

00:29:17.020 --> 00:29:22.380
And then, max-- you know,
let's start with width.

00:29:22.380 --> 00:29:24.960
Width is 500 pixels.

00:29:29.470 --> 00:29:32.713
So now, things are pretty much
in the center, which is nice.

00:29:32.713 --> 00:29:33.630
That's the nice thing.

00:29:33.630 --> 00:29:37.270
Fluid page will automatically
keep itself centered,

00:29:37.270 --> 00:29:38.460
which is nice.

00:29:38.460 --> 00:29:44.440
If it didn't, we would have to
[INAUDIBLE] control [AUDIO OUT]

00:29:44.440 --> 00:29:45.310
that.

00:29:45.310 --> 00:29:54.350
The problem that we run into is,
equals, that will cause issues.

00:29:54.350 --> 00:29:58.360
And so we don't
actually want width.

00:29:58.360 --> 00:30:03.130
We want max width.

00:30:03.130 --> 00:30:09.010
And so max width says, follow
the width of the page--

00:30:09.010 --> 00:30:13.420
the width of your iPhone screen
or your computer screen--

00:30:13.420 --> 00:30:15.730
unless that's bigger
than 500 pixels.

00:30:15.730 --> 00:30:18.670
So most of the time, that's
going to be bigger than 500

00:30:18.670 --> 00:30:19.820
pixels.

00:30:19.820 --> 00:30:21.310
But in the case
where it's smaller,

00:30:21.310 --> 00:30:25.010
it will let it shrink,
at least in theory.

00:30:25.010 --> 00:30:30.980
So let's just to see if that
does what I said it would.

00:30:30.980 --> 00:30:32.390
So yeah, it's shrinking now.

00:30:32.390 --> 00:30:34.670
It's not letting
itself get too big.

00:30:34.670 --> 00:30:36.350
So that's nice.

00:30:36.350 --> 00:30:37.310
So cool.

00:30:37.310 --> 00:30:39.968
It's looking pretty
