This is another one
of those-- you have

00:31:10.190 --> 00:31:13.193
to look it up a million times.

00:31:13.193 --> 00:31:14.610
I got it right on
the first guess.

00:31:14.610 --> 00:31:17.340
I'd almost never done that.

00:31:17.340 --> 00:31:19.680
If you look at that
CSS Grid cheat sheet,

00:31:19.680 --> 00:31:21.810
there's a bunch
of different ways

00:31:21.810 --> 00:31:28.830
to align the things
in your grid.

00:31:28.830 --> 00:31:31.000
And yeah, so here we go.

00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:31.980
So justify.

00:31:31.980 --> 00:31:34.740
And you can justify as self.

00:31:34.740 --> 00:31:37.320
We could justify items.

00:31:37.320 --> 00:31:39.750
So you get lucky, basically.

00:31:39.750 --> 00:31:41.723
Almost no one ever remembers it.

00:31:41.723 --> 00:31:43.390
But I got lucky and
remembered it there.

00:31:43.390 --> 00:31:47.440
So now, this is lined up, which
the way that it should be.

00:31:47.440 --> 00:31:48.720
So that's good.

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:52.630
Let's do one more guess,
just to make sure.

00:31:52.630 --> 00:31:54.070
Cool, it's working
how it should.

00:31:54.070 --> 00:31:56.650
That's nice.

00:31:56.650 --> 00:32:01.930
So I think the last
thing that I want to do

00:32:01.930 --> 00:32:06.880
is, fix this input so that the
input is the Go button that's

00:32:06.880 --> 00:32:10.640
here, because we're just
kind of wasting space.

00:32:10.640 --> 00:32:12.340
So to do that like
we had before,

00:32:12.340 --> 00:32:14.920
when we had the letters
that just stacked

00:32:14.920 --> 00:32:19.950
on top of each other, it's
because they're just this block

00:32:19.950 --> 00:32:20.940
setup.

00:32:20.940 --> 00:32:24.030
We don't actually let
them know that we want

00:32:24.030 --> 00:32:27.580
them to be next to each other.

00:32:27.580 --> 00:32:30.660
And so we can
group them together

00:32:30.660 --> 00:32:33.270
just by wrapping them in a div.

00:32:33.270 --> 00:32:34.410
So we can say, div.

00:32:34.410 --> 00:32:36.078
This is just [INAUDIBLE].

00:32:36.078 --> 00:32:37.245
Bring them up into that div.

00:32:39.950 --> 00:32:42.630
So this shouldn't change
anything right now.

00:32:42.630 --> 00:32:43.130
It didn't.

00:32:43.130 --> 00:32:45.450
So they're still right there.

00:32:45.450 --> 00:32:48.350
Let's give this div a class so
that we can start targeting it

00:32:48.350 --> 00:32:51.220
with our CSS.

00:32:51.220 --> 00:32:53.225
Say, input wrapper.

00:32:56.520 --> 00:32:57.780
Make sure that we're--

00:33:00.390 --> 00:33:07.590
take that input wrapper
down here-- .input wrapper.

00:33:07.590 --> 00:33:10.066
outline 1px solid.

00:33:14.810 --> 00:33:17.180
Let's just do forest green.

00:33:17.180 --> 00:33:21.210
There's only so many CSS
colors I can keep in my head.

00:33:21.210 --> 00:33:21.710
Cool.

00:33:21.710 --> 00:33:26.640
So now we see that we
do have this div there.

00:33:26.640 --> 00:33:29.920
And we have the individual
elements within it.

00:33:29.920 --> 00:33:35.940
So like we did before, we
could do, display, grid.

00:33:35.940 --> 00:33:38.600
See what that gives us.

00:33:38.600 --> 00:33:41.000
Does not exactly do
what we might want.

00:33:45.170 --> 00:33:52.330
But let's do a different way.

00:33:52.330 --> 00:33:54.190
Let's do display, flex.

00:33:54.190 --> 00:33:59.140
And Flexbox is another
layout algorithm.

00:33:59.140 --> 00:34:00.820
Now they're next to each other.

00:34:00.820 --> 00:34:03.520
Flexbox is,
basically, if you want

00:34:03.520 --> 00:34:05.020
to line things up
next to each other

00:34:05.020 --> 00:34:07.120
and make them align
in the proper way,

00:34:07.120 --> 00:34:10.969
Flexbox is what you want to use.

00:34:10.969 --> 00:34:14.650
So this is a kind of a
perfect scenario for Flexbox.

00:34:14.650 --> 00:34:18.949
So a couple of things stand
out as not good right now.

00:34:18.949 --> 00:34:23.242
One is, the Go button is
really tall compared to this.

00:34:23.242 --> 00:34:25.409
And then, also, they're
right up next to each other.

00:34:25.409 --> 00:34:28.239
I don't think we want
them next to each other.

00:34:28.239 --> 00:34:34.050
So let's do that same
way of selecting a child.

00:34:34.050 --> 00:34:35.580
So we could say, input wrapper.

00:34:35.580 --> 00:34:40.190
And then, button,
which is the element,

00:34:40.190 --> 00:34:41.360
selecting a button element.

00:34:41.360 --> 00:34:45.469
We could just say,
margin left, and give it

00:34:45.469 --> 00:34:47.730
something like 10 pixels.

00:34:47.730 --> 00:34:49.520
So in theory, that
should take this button

00:34:49.520 --> 00:34:52.639
and basically make it
10 pixels from the thing

00:34:52.639 --> 00:34:54.870
that it's closest
to on the left.

00:34:54.870 --> 00:34:55.370
Did.

00:34:55.370 --> 00:34:57.290
So that's nice.

00:34:57.290 --> 00:34:58.250
So that's better.

00:34:58.250 --> 00:35:02.330
But now, I don't like that
they're like this at all.

00:35:02.330 --> 00:35:03.590
That's kind of gross.

00:35:03.590 --> 00:35:09.320
So what we can do is, go
into our browser's DevTools.

00:35:09.320 --> 00:35:12.620
Because just like
CSS Grid, CSS Flexbox

00:35:12.620 --> 00:35:16.640
has all sorts of fun settings
that no one ever remembers.

00:35:16.640 --> 00:35:20.690
But the DevTools
tools within Chrome

00:35:20.690 --> 00:35:23.210
have a nice little tool
for working with them.

00:35:23.210 --> 00:35:26.240
So you can do things
like align your content.

00:35:26.240 --> 00:35:29.750
And you just play with this
little thing right here,

00:35:29.750 --> 00:35:32.660
and make it look
like want it to.

00:35:32.660 --> 00:35:35.210
So let's do-- that centered it.

00:35:35.210 --> 00:35:37.400
So I would say,
justify-content, space around.

00:35:37.400 --> 00:35:40.920
align-content doesn't
do anything for us.

00:35:40.920 --> 00:35:42.740
So we can kind of
just ignore it.

00:35:42.740 --> 00:35:44.090
align-item center.

00:35:44.090 --> 00:35:46.640
So now they're pretty
close to being centered.

00:35:49.870 --> 00:35:54.855
So I'm going to copy
this CSS from here.

00:35:59.100 --> 00:36:03.380
Put it here so I don't forget
it, because I will forget it.

00:36:03.380 --> 00:36:05.750
Quickly make sure that it works.

00:36:05.750 --> 00:36:07.250
OK, it did.

00:36:07.250 --> 00:36:09.440
Let's go back in here again.

00:36:09.440 --> 00:36:10.440
That looks pretty good.

00:36:10.440 --> 00:36:11.990
But if you're like
me, you're going

00:36:11.990 --> 00:36:14.900
to get driven insane by the
fact that this button is not

00:36:14.900 --> 00:36:24.820
actually lined up with
the input, the text input.

00:36:24.820 --> 00:36:28.380
And that's because you can
see that there's this weird--

00:36:28.380 --> 00:36:30.813
there's a margin on the bottom
of that input that is not

00:36:30.813 --> 00:36:31.980
on the bottom of the button.

00:36:31.980 --> 00:36:35.700
And so that causes
it to be misaligned.

00:36:35.700 --> 00:36:41.070
And so what we can do
is, since we already

00:36:41.070 --> 00:36:44.988
have something targeting
the button, go back in here,

00:36:44.988 --> 00:36:45.530
look at this.

00:36:45.530 --> 00:36:50.230
So it's a shiny input
container form group.

00:36:50.230 --> 00:36:52.060
It's a div.

00:36:52.060 --> 00:36:58.270
So what we could do is, say,
let me get, in my input-wrapper,

00:36:58.270 --> 00:36:58.905
div.

00:36:58.905 --> 00:37:01.030
So this is saying, I'm
going to target the div that

00:37:01.030 --> 00:37:03.460
is the child of input-wrapper.

00:37:03.460 --> 00:37:06.140
So that should be
this text input.

00:37:06.140 --> 00:37:10.168
And then we could just
say, margin-bottom is 0.

00:37:10.168 --> 00:37:11.710
Don't need to put
pixels or anything,

00:37:11.710 --> 00:37:14.110
because zero doesn't need units.

00:37:14.110 --> 00:37:15.520
Reload it.

00:37:15.520 --> 00:37:17.950
And now it sticks there.

00:37:17.950 --> 00:37:20.500
So at least it's lined
up on the bottom.

00:37:23.800 --> 00:37:28.960
I think we do
align-items, flex-end.

00:37:28.960 --> 00:37:31.540
And this-- OK.

00:37:31.540 --> 00:37:34.690
So flex-end says, in
your vertical alignment

00:37:34.690 --> 00:37:38.500
of these items in this
box, put it at the end.

00:37:38.500 --> 00:37:41.020
You have to prefix
it with flex here,

00:37:41.020 --> 00:37:44.110
because older
browsers need that.

00:37:44.110 --> 00:37:46.690
Newer browsers, you
could just say, end.

00:37:46.690 --> 00:37:48.070
They also understand flex-end.

00:37:48.070 --> 00:37:50.750
So it's safe to put that there.

00:37:50.750 --> 00:37:54.910
So now, we pretty
much got what we want.

00:37:54.910 --> 00:37:57.190
They're lined up
how we want them.

00:37:57.190 --> 00:38:02.990
And then, we can--

00:38:02.990 --> 00:38:05.918
actually, justify-content space
around is not what we want,

00:38:05.918 --> 00:38:07.710
because we already
spaced those things out.

00:38:07.710 --> 00:38:10.980
So let's put it,
justify-content as center.

00:38:10.980 --> 00:38:12.000
So now they're centered.

00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:14.460
The button, the space that we
already did with our margin,

00:38:14.460 --> 00:38:15.960
is there.

00:38:15.960 --> 00:38:16.977
So that's nice.

00:38:16.977 --> 00:38:18.810
And then, we've just
got to get rid of this.

00:38:18.810 --> 00:38:22.980
There's a space on the top of
this, but not on the bottom.

00:38:22.980 --> 00:38:26.220
So we dealt with that before
by putting padding on it.

00:38:26.220 --> 00:38:28.530
So let's just say, padding--

00:38:28.530 --> 00:38:31.150
we only need padding
on the bottom here.

00:38:31.150 --> 00:38:31.985
10 pixels.

00:38:34.895 --> 00:38:35.395
Cool.

00:38:35.395 --> 00:38:37.270
And then, take out this outline.

00:38:40.260 --> 00:38:47.980
And OK, let's see.

00:38:47.980 --> 00:38:51.320
Run tests.

00:38:51.320 --> 00:38:55.950
That is looking pretty decent.

00:38:55.950 --> 00:39:01.290
We got to fix-- got to get
rid of that one outline

00:39:01.290 --> 00:39:04.380
that I was so eagerly adding.

00:39:04.380 --> 00:39:10.350
Now we're-- helps to actually
look at it how it will be,

00:39:10.350 --> 00:39:13.920
just to make sure that there's
not some weird CSS funkiness

00:39:13.920 --> 00:39:14.470
going on.

00:39:14.470 --> 00:39:16.420
So that's pretty good.

00:39:16.420 --> 00:39:20.660
I think the thing
that I would do next

00:39:20.660 --> 00:39:22.130
is, these colors are not right.

00:39:22.130 --> 00:39:26.430
That's orange-red is like
very in-your-face aggressive.

00:39:26.430 --> 00:39:31.790
So I will just go and use this
handy-dandy CSS inspector tool

00:39:31.790 --> 00:39:33.470
that I've been using.

00:39:33.470 --> 00:39:34.445
Go to the Wordle app.

00:39:39.250 --> 00:39:41.210
Daily word game.

00:39:41.210 --> 00:39:43.040
And so we see that
these are the colors.

00:39:43.040 --> 00:39:47.170
And we can just do
that Inspect Element.

00:39:47.170 --> 00:39:51.160
And then, background color
of our color, correct.

00:39:51.160 --> 00:39:53.800
But there's an easier way
to [AUDIO OUT] colors.

00:39:53.800 --> 00:39:58.240
Or some might say, steal colors.

00:39:58.240 --> 00:39:59.260
So we use this, you see?

00:39:59.260 --> 00:40:00.775
This little eyedropper.

00:40:00.775 --> 00:40:02.290
Put that eyedropper
over something.

00:40:02.290 --> 00:40:03.820
It'll show up the
color right there.

00:40:03.820 --> 00:40:06.290
We can copy that.

00:40:06.290 --> 00:40:10.280
So forest green gets
replaced by this hex color.

00:40:10.280 --> 00:40:15.080
And then, the gray that
he uses is this hex color.

00:40:18.080 --> 00:40:21.150
And last, this is
hardly an orange.

00:40:21.150 --> 00:40:24.950
It's more like goldenrod, maybe.

00:40:24.950 --> 00:40:26.680
Use that.

00:40:26.680 --> 00:40:27.460
Reload it.

00:40:27.460 --> 00:40:28.520
That looks correct.

00:40:28.520 --> 00:40:34.540
So cool.

00:40:34.540 --> 00:40:36.910
I think that's pretty good.

00:40:40.080 --> 00:40:43.200
Maybe one thing that we could
do is make the text bold.

00:40:43.200 --> 00:40:45.870
So font-weight, bold.

00:40:45.870 --> 00:40:48.690
Make it pop out a
little bit more.

00:40:48.690 --> 00:40:50.010
Kind of gets lost as a--

00:40:58.880 --> 00:40:59.390
cool.

00:40:59.390 --> 00:41:04.040
I think that gets us pretty far.

00:41:04.040 --> 00:41:06.920
We could tackle this keyboard,
but we would basically

00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:11.090
just repeat the same steps
that we did for this.

00:41:11.090 --> 00:41:15.460
Just turn everything into a
div and lay it out properly.

